{"name":"Eiderdown","hex":"#e6dbc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eiderdown","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The down of the eider duck, used for stuffing pillows and quilts.","A quilt stuffed with this down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eiderdown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common eider","blocks":[{"text":"The common eider, also called St. Cuthbert's duck or Cuddy's duck, is a large sea-duck that is distributed over the northern coasts of Europe, North America and eastern Siberia. It breeds in Arctic and some northern temperate regions, but winters somewhat farther south in temperate zones, when it can form large flocks on coastal waters. It can fly at speeds up to 113 km/h (70 mph)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/%D0%9F%D1%83%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%9A%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%B1%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B9_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%96.jpg/330px-%D0%9F%D1%83%D1%85%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%9A%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%B1%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B9_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%96.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_eider"},{"title":"Duvet","blocks":[{"text":"A duvet, usually called a comforter or (down-filled) quilt in American English, and a doona in Australian English, is a type of bedding consisting of a soft flat bag filled with down, feathers, wool, cotton, silk, or a synthetic alternative, and is typically protected with a removable cover, similar to a pillow and pillow case. Sleepers often use a duvet without a top bed sheet, as the duvet cover can readily be removed and laundered as often as the bottom sheet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/La_cama_deshecha_%282724466831%29.jpg/330px-La_cama_deshecha_%282724466831%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https